# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recorded media and derived tensors NEVER enter git.
#
# A repo that has once held large binaries stays bloated permanently: the blobs
# live in history even after deletion, and every future clone pays for them.
# Recorded media is backed up separately (external drive + offsite copy).
#
# What IS versioned: code, configs, and the small text files whose history is
# the point -- manifest.csv, signers.csv, and the gloss prompt list. Those are
# whitelisted with ! rules below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw video, in any location
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm

# Cached landmark tensors
*.npy
*.npz

# Data directories (recorded takes, extracted landmarks, archival copies)
data/
!msl/data/
raw/
archive/
landmark_cache/

# Re-admit the dataset record itself: small, text, and its history matters.
!**/manifest.csv
!**/signers.csv
!**/prompts/**/*.txt
!**/prompts/**/*.csv

# MediaPipe model bundles: downloaded once, 13.7 MB of binary, not ours to ship.
assets/
*.task

# Model artifacts
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
checkpoints/
runs/
outputs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One narrow exception, walked down level by level.
#
# A `!` rule cannot re-admit a file whose parent directory is excluded -- git
# never descends into an excluded directory to see it. So `data/` above makes
# the `!**/manifest.csv` whitelist unreachable for anything under the data root,
# and re-admitting one file means un-excluding each directory on its path and
# re-excluding that directory's other contents.
#
# extract_log_firstpass.csv is the ONLY surviving record of per-clip source
# width/height/fps for the WLASL100 corpus. Spec S4 requires aspect ratio per
# clip, and a cache-only extraction run cannot reproduce these columns -- the
# tensor does not store them. It is 184 KB of text and it is not regenerable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!data/
data/*
!data/wlasl/
data/wlasl/*
!data/wlasl/extract_log_firstpass.csv
!data/wlasl/download_log_100.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sweep metrics, and only those. Same parent-directory rule as the data logs:
# `runs/` above excludes the tree, so a `!` rule cannot reach into it. The idiom
# is to re-include the DIRECTORIES (a trailing slash matches directories only)
# so git descends, then whitelist the one filename.
#
# sweep_metrics.json is small text whose history is the point -- it is the
# record of what each variant scored at each seed. Checkpoints, figures and
# .npy confusion matrices stay ignored: reproducible bulk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!runs/
runs/**
!runs/**/
!**/sweep_metrics.json
